# Preserve working logic (LiVi)

## Hard rule

Current app behavior is considered **correct and must stay working**.
Optimize **responsiveness / latency only**. Do **not** change product logic, call/chat/PiP semantics, or welcome design unless the user explicitly asks.

## Do not break

- Random search → `RandomChat`
- Friends add/remove, chats, call log
- Outgoing/incoming call flow: dial, cancel, redial, accept, reject, hangup
- Call lock, crown/profile, welcome tabs
- In-app PiP and Android system PiP enter/exit/end
- Audio route behavior that already works (earpiece/speaker/headset) — tune timing, don’t rewrite policy

## Performance work priorities (agreed)

1. Cancel → immediate redial (“Вызов” starts again without sticky busy)
2. Instant welcome/sidebar navigation taps
3. Accept → VideoCall transition (later)
4. In-app PiP enter/exit (**last**)

## How to change code

- Prefer removing artificial waits / busy holds / duplicate cancel / heavy sync work on the happy path
- Keep race guards that protect real edge cases; only shorten or scope them when proven to block UI
- Minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors; no “simplify the whole call stack”
- Do **not** commit or push unless the user explicitly asks

## Regression check after any perf patch

Manually verify: cancel→redial, tab switches, accept/hangup still connect and clean up, PiP still works if touched.
